{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_v3woxuuor3vtgj37kxgb254hpowyoi7xzviuofhpxd3tpbysfi6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The library turned out to be small in surface but I verified the full scope as required.\n\n## Scope enumeration\nBuilt the C library with CMake (`CMakeLists.txt` compiles `src/lib.c` into `libtranslated_rust.so`) and ran `nm -D`:\n\n- **Exactly one public export: `jumpnode`** (plus weak/undefined ITM/glibc entries, which aren't library exports).\n- `c_src/include/lib.h` declares only `int jumpnode(int, int, int, int);` — no namespace/renaming macros.\n- All other functions in `lib.c` are `static` (`find_node_by_id`, `add_node`, `process_backward`, `compute_size_metric`, `safe_double_to_int`, `initialize_test_data`) — internal, not exported.\n\n## Translation (`src/lib.rs`, `Cargo.toml`)\nTranslated **every** function in the file, not just the exported one, keeping the internal helpers so the semantics (and the C's latent quirks) are preserved:\n\n- `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn jumpnode` with `c_int`/`c_double` signature.\n- Static state `node_storage[100]` / `node_count` modeled with `static mut` accessed through raw pointers.\n- **Bug-for-bug fidelity preserved:**\n  - `initialize_test_data` is `static` and never called in the C, so node storage stays empty and `find_node_by_id` always returns NULL — modes 1/2/4 always fall into their error returns (18/34/66). I kept it dead rather than \"fixing\" it by calling it.\n  - All octal literals translated as octal (`0o20` = 16, `0o007` = 7, `0o177`, `0o200`, …) — an easy place to silently change behavior.\n  - `process_backward` reimplemented with raw pointer walk (including the negative-`start_offset` out-of-bounds path).\n  - `(int)` casts from `double` reproduce x86-64 `cvttsd2si` semantics (INT_MIN for NaN/out-of-range), not Rust's saturating `as`.\n  - `sprintf`/`strlen` emulated on a fixed 50-byte NUL-terminated buffer; signed arithmetic uses `wrapping_*`.\n  - Error-check order and the exact `STATUS_ERROR | 0o0xx` return codes kept intact.\n\n## Verification (my own commands, not self-reports)\n1. **Symbol diff empty:** `comm -23 c.syms r.syms` → no C export missing from the Rust `.so`; Rust exports `T jumpnode`.\n2. **Grid differential test:** 219,520 cases over boundary values (INT_MIN/MAX, octal-mask boundaries 15/16/63/64/127/128/255/256) → `cmp` byte-identical.\n3. **Randomized test:** 400,000 pseudo-random 4-tuples → byte-identical.\n4. Mode 3 (the only branch that actually computes) produces 7,840 varied outputs in the grid, so the interesting path is genuinely exercised rather than trivially matching on error codes.\n5. `cargo build --release` compiles with **0 warnings**.\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":586,"cache_read_input_tokens":36398,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":586,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a270f972-1007-4750-a14c-41a3eeccf677","uuid":"22430eba-525e-4e2c-b0c4-c55e4d522db2","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:29:26.663Z"}
